---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Band from '../components/Band.astro';
import TermTip from '../components/TermTip.astro';
import SideCard from '../components/SideCard.astro';
import ProofChips from '../components/ProofChips.astro';
import GapCards from '../components/GapCards.astro';
import ScenarioCards from '../components/ScenarioCards.astro';
import NumberFlip from '../components/NumberFlip.astro';
import ShotFrame from '../components/ShotFrame.astro';
import MoreBox from '../components/MoreBox.astro';
import GapMeter from '../components/GapMeter.astro';
import StatChips from '../components/StatChips.astro';
import PullLine from '../components/PullLine.astro';
import ValueTiles from '../components/ValueTiles.astro';
import EmailSignup from '../components/EmailSignup.astro';
import ScrollProgress from '../components/ScrollProgress.astro';
import FirmFitPicker from '../components/FirmFitPicker.astro';
import FirmCard from '../components/FirmCard.astro';
import { getFirm } from '../config/firms';
import { site } from '../config/site';
import payout from '../assets/proof/apex-payout-2026-08-12.png';
import calendarShot from '../assets/proof/nfp-calendar-2026-08-07.png';
import fvgShot from '../assets/proof/mnq-fvg-entry-2026-08-07.png';
import executionShot from '../assets/proof/tradovate-execution-2026-08-07.png';

const fundednext = getFirm('fundednext')!;
const apex = getFirm('apex')!;

// Copy comes from 03-content/drafts/start-from-zero.md, pieces 1 to 7.
// Lines marked PLACEHOLDER are not in Aayush's words yet. Listed in 03-content/front-page/placeholders.md.
---
<BaseLayout showFooterSignup={false}>
  <ScrollProgress />
  <!-- Piece 1. First screen -->
  <Band>
    <div class="hero">
      <div class="stack left">
        <div class="label">Macro · Futures · From India</div>
        <h1 class="h-hero">Know what's priced in. Trade what changes.</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          I'm Aayush. I trade Nasdaq futures from India. Before every big number, I know what the market already expects, so it's already{' '}
          <TermTip title="Priced in" text="Priced in means the market already expects it. The expected number does not move price. The surprise does.">priced in</TermTip>.
          When the number surprises, I trade it.
        </p>
        <ProofChips
          chips={[{ text: '102 points' }, { text: '4 MNQ' }, { text: 'Apex payout', proof: true }]}
          proofTitle="Apex payout, $1,446"
          proofNote="This is from that week, not one trade. I traded 3 to 4 more days after it."
          proofImage={payout}
          proofAlt="Apex Trader Funding rewards certificate, $1,446, approved on 12 August 2026"
        />
      </div>
      <div class="stack right">
        <!-- PLACEHOLDER: both side cards, not in Aayush's words yet -->
        <SideCard href="/macro" label="The macro side" title="I read the news before the chart">
          NFP, CPI, the Fed.<br />I watch gold and the dollar too. I don't trade them.
        </SideCard>
        <!-- PLACEHOLDER -->
        <SideCard href="/journal" label="The futures side" title="I trade Nasdaq futures">
          Mostly MNQ, on funded accounts. The number gives me direction. The 1 minute chart gives me my entry.
        </SideCard>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Band>

  <!-- Piece 2. The gap -->
  <Band variant="white">
    <div class="stack gap">
      <div class="stack intro">
        <div class="label">The gap</div>
        <!-- PLACEHOLDER: heading and the line under it -->
        <h2 class="h-sec">Most people learn one side.</h2>
        <p class="lead">Some learn only the chart. Some only read the news. Both feel stuck in the same place.</p>
      </div>
      <GapCards
        cards={[
          { title: 'Chart only', text: "You learn setups. FVG, order blocks. But at 6 PM price moves 300 points and you don't know why." },
          { title: 'News only', text: 'You read headlines. Jobs weak, Fed this, Fed that. But nobody shows you the trade.' },
          { title: 'From India', text: "You can't easily trade US futures from here. Prop firms are the way in. I show you which ones, honestly." },
          { title: 'Here', text: 'The number tells me the direction. The chart tells me where to get in. I show you both, on real trades.', highlight: true },
        ]}
      />
      <!-- PLACEHOLDER: punch line -->
      <p class="punch">The money is where they meet. Here is one real night.</p>
    </div>
  </Band>

  <!-- Piece 3. One real night -->
  <Band>
    <div class="read stack night">
      <div class="label">One real night</div>
      <h2 class="h-sec">Friday 7 August. 6 PM India time.</h2>
      <p>That week, everyone was on the same side. The market thought the Fed would raise rates in September. Then a weak ADP report came and two hikes became one.</p>
      <p>Gold ran <span class="n">6%</span> in a week. Nasdaq just sat there, waiting. Same story, two different markets.</p>
      <p>I don't guess on days like this. The day before, I write three scenarios.</p>

      <ScenarioCards
        scenarios={[
          { condition: 'Near 85K', direction: 'flat', meaning: 'Priced in. Nothing changes.' },
          { condition: '150K or more', direction: 'down', meaning: 'Nasdaq falls hard.' },
          { condition: 'Below 40K', direction: 'up', meaning: 'Nasdaq rises.', happened: true },
        ]}
      />

      <p>Then I wait. After NFP, I never trade the number itself. Fills can slip <span class="n">50 to 100</span> points in that window. That is gambling, not trading. I wait for new price action after the data, and let that show me the direction.</p>

      <NumberFlip
        label="NFP · The numbers"
        from={85}
        to={-23}
        unit="K"
        caption="Jobs added. The market expected 85K."
        rows={[
          { label: 'Forecast', value: '85K' },
          { label: 'Previous', value: '20K' },
          { label: 'Unemployment', value: '4.1%' },
        ]}
        directions={[
          { name: 'NQ', direction: 'up' },
          { name: 'Gold', direction: 'up' },
        ]}
      />

      <p>The US lost jobs. Weak jobs means fewer rate hikes. Fewer hikes is good for Nasdaq and gold. My scenario had already told me this.</p>

      <ShotFrame
        id="shot-calendar"
        src={calendarShot}
        alt="Economic calendar for Friday 7 August. Non-Farm Employment Change: actual minus 23K, forecast 85K, previous 20K."
        caption="NFP calendar. Actual −23K, forecast 85K, previous 20K."
      />

      <MoreBox title="Why do gold and Nasdaq move together here?">
        Both were trading the same story, the rate hike story. Fewer hikes means cheaper money later. That helps both. Most days they don't move together. This week they did, because one thing drove both.
      </MoreBox>

      <p>Here is what most people miss. The number was huge. But the move was small.</p>

      <GapMeter
        label="Room left"
        usual={{ text: 'Usual move on a surprise this big', value: '~300 pts', pct: 100 }}
        night={{ text: 'This night', value: '~100 to 150 pts', pct: 42 }}
        note="Room left"
      />

      <p>So the market was not done. There was still room. If it had moved <span class="n">300</span> already, I would not have taken this trade.</p>
      <p>A few minutes later, a gap formed on the 1 minute chart. I entered inside it, at <span class="n">6:04 PM</span>. Stop below it.</p>

      <ShotFrame
        id="shot-fvg"
        src={fvgShot}
        alt="TradingView, E-mini Nasdaq 1 minute chart. A bullish fair value gap with the entry inside it and the previous day high at 29,686.25 marked."
        caption="TradingView, NQ 1 minute. Bullish FVG, entry inside it. Target: the 1 hour draw on liquidity. Previous day high 29,686.25 is visible."
        tall
      />

      <MoreBox title="What is an FVG?">
        A gap price leaves behind when it moves too fast. Price often comes back to it, then continues.
      </MoreBox>

      <StatChips chips={['4 MNQ', '102 points', '~$600']} />

      <ShotFrame
        id="shot-execution"
        src={executionShot}
        alt="Tradovate chart on 7 August at 6:35 PM showing the entry, the partial and the exit marked on a strong rise."
        caption="Execution on Tradovate. The entry, the partial and the exit, marked on the chart."
        tall
      />

      <p>One contract came off early. Three ran the full <span class="n">102</span>. I don't remember my exact stop. It was an old trade and I have no data, so I won't make one up.</p>

      <PullLine>Read the size of the reaction against the size of the surprise.</PullLine>
    </div>
  </Band>

  <!-- Piece 4. The honest part -->
  <Band variant="wine">
    <div class="read stack honest">
      <div class="label">The honest part</div>
      <h2 class="h-sec">This night was rare.</h2>
      <p>Most releases land near the forecast. Then price just chops, up and down, taking everyone's stops. That is okay.</p>
      <p>About <span class="n">90%</span> of days, I can't read the direction. I take my 1 to 1 and go home. About <span class="n">10%</span> of days are clear. 7 August was one.</p>
      <p>The difference between a small win and <span class="n">102</span> points was not my chart reading. It was whether the news was readable.</p>
      <p>Some days you don't need a thesis. You just need to read the number and respect the direction.</p>
    </div>
  </Band>

  <!-- Piece 5. What you get here -->
  <Band variant="white">
    <div class="stack gap">
      <div class="stack intro">
        <div class="label">What you get here</div>
        <h2 class="h-sec">Everything on this site comes back to one question.</h2>
        <!-- PLACEHOLDER: the four tiles are not in Aayush's words yet -->
        <p class="lead">What is priced in, and what would change it?</p>
      </div>
      <ValueTiles
        tiles={[
          { title: 'Macro Desk', text: 'What is priced in before every big event. Scenarios written before the number.', href: '/macro' },
          { title: 'Learn', text: 'The news and the chart together, in simple words.', href: '/learn' },
          { title: 'Journal', text: 'My real trades. Wins and losses, with numbers.', href: '/journal' },
          { title: 'Start here', text: 'Trading futures from India with prop firms. Honest notes on each.', href: '/start-here' },
        ]}
      />
    </div>
  </Band>

  <!-- Email band, per BUILD-PLAN section 5 -->
  <Band variant="wine">
    <EmailSignup variant="wine" id="email-home" />
  </Band>

  <!-- Piece 6. Futures from India -->
  <Band>
    <div class="read stack india">
      <div class="label">Start here</div>
      <h2 class="h-sec">How do I do this from India?</h2>
      <p>Prop firms give you their money to trade after you pass a test. You keep a share of the profit. If you fail, you lose the fee, not your savings.</p>
      <p>Which one fits depends on you.</p>

      <FirmFitPicker newLabel="I'm new" edgeLabel="I know my edge">
        <FirmCard slot="new" firm={fundednext} href="/go/fundednext" ctaLabel="See FundedNext">
          <p>My pick for beginners. Small 5K and 10K accounts, so you can trade Nasdaq as a CFD without much at stake. Futures with end of day drawdown too. In my opinion the payout structure is great.</p>
        </FirmCard>
        <FirmCard
          slot="edge"
          firm={apex}
          href={apex.url ?? '/start-here'}
          ctaLabel="ApexTraderFunding.com"
          disclosure="Not an affiliate link. I'm not affiliated with Apex."
        >
          <p>My payout came from here. But it is not for beginners. The drawdown is intraday and it follows your open profit. Say a trade goes to 2.5R, then falls back to breakeven. You made nothing, but your drawdown still ate away.</p>
        </FirmCard>
      </FirmFitPicker>

      <p>For the macro side, I open MRKT every morning. It shows me what is priced in, and which events carry more weight right now. It saves me hours on Nasdaq.</p>
      <p>
        <a class="btn" href="/go/mrkt" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener">See MRKT</a>
      </p>
      <p class="ui fine">MRKT is an affiliate link. I earn a commission if you sign up. I use it daily either way. This is my honest opinion, not advice.</p>
    </div>
  </Band>

  <!-- Piece 7. The ending -->
  <Band>
    <div class="read stack ending">
      <p class="lead">Before every big number, I write my scenarios. Same as I did on 7 August. They live on the Macro Desk.</p>
      <p><a class="btn" href="/macro">Open the Macro Desk</a></p>
      <p class="signoff">{site.signOff}</p>
    </div>
  </Band>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.25fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 64px; align-items: start; margin-top: -14px; } /* band padding is 110px, the reference hero starts at 96px */
  .left { gap: 24px; }
  .left .lead { max-width: 560px; }
  .right { gap: 16px; padding-top: 30px; }
  .gap { gap: 36px; }
  .intro { gap: 14px; max-width: 680px; }
  .night, .honest, .india, .ending { gap: 28px; }
  .night > p, .honest > p, .india > p { max-width: 68ch; }
  .night :global(.numcard), .night :global(.meter) { margin: 4px 0; }
  .fine { font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .signoff { font-family: var(--font-number); font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-muted); padding-top: 18px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .punch { font-family: var(--font-heading); font-weight: 600; font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.3; color: var(--ink); }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 28px; margin-top: 0; }
    .left { gap: 20px; }
    .right { padding-top: 0; }
    .punch { font-size: 21px; }
  }
</style>
